$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Hiyama Coupling of Aryl Bromides and Chlorides.
A 10 mL vial was charged with 3 mmol of TBAF• xH2O (794 mg), 0.5 mol % of
Pd(OAc)2 (2.24 mg), and 1.0 mol%of ligand 1 (10.03 mg) in a glovebox. The
vial was capped and brought outside the glovebox where 4 mmol of
arylsiloxane and 2 mmol of aryl halide were added under an argon flow.
The reaction vessel was heated to 80 °C for the specified times given in
the tables. The mixtures were then purified by column chromatography
(0-5% EtOAc). Pure biaryls. entry 10 yield a (%) 93
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM Hiyama cross-coupling, no solvent
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Advantageous Use of tBu2P-N=P(iBuNCH2CH2)3N in the Hiyama Coupling of
Aryl Bromides and Chlorides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Raders, Steven M.; Kingston, Jesudoss V.; Verkade, John G.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2010), 75(5), 1744-1747

