$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):SOL(1):CAS_RN
$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM General Procedure for the Preparation of Pd Nanoparticle and Catalysis of
Hiyama Coupling Reaction. A weighed amount of K2PdCl4 (13 mg, 0.04 mmol)
and PEG 600 (700 mg, 1.16 mmol) was heated at 70 °C for 15 min to
complete the formation of Pd nanoparticles. To this suspension of
colloidal Pd at ambient temperature were added aryltrialkoxysilane (2
mmol), benzyl halide (1 mmol), and tetrabutylammonium fluoride The
reaction mixture was allowed to cool at room temperature, and THF was
removed. The residue was extracted with ether (15 mL x 3), and the
combined organic extract was dried over anhydrous Na2SO4 and concentrated
in vacuum. The residue thus obtained was subjected to flash column
chromatography on silica gel (230-400 mesh) with either petroleum ether
or ethyl acetate (2-10%) in petroleum ether as eluent. Diphenylmethane
(2a): 3 1H NMR (300 MHz, CDCl3): δ 4.05 (s, 2H), 7.25-7.27 (m, 6H),
7.33-7.38 (m, 4H); 13C NMR (75 MHz, CDCl3): δ 42.05, 126.18, 128.57,
129.05, 141.22.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):NOTES
$DATUM alternative preparation shown, Hiyama coupling; PEG-600 used (stage 1)
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Palladium Nanoparticle Catalyzed Hiyama Coupling Reaction of Benzyl
Halides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Srimani, Dipankar; Bej, Ansuman; Sarkar, Amitabha
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of Organic Chemistry (2010), 75(12), 4296-4299

