$DATUM 109-99-9
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):EXP_PROC
$DATUM Cross-Coupling Procedure with [HP(t-Bu)2Me]BF4. In the air, PdBr2 (10.6
mg, 0.040 mmol) and [HP(t-Bu)2Me]BF4 (24.8 mg, 0.10 mmol) were placed in
a vial equipped with a stir bar. The vial was closed with a septum
screw-cap, and then it was evacuated and refilled with argon (three
times). THF (2.4 mL) and TBAF (0.10 mL, 0.10 mmol) were added, and the
resulting mixture was stirred vigorously for 30 minutes at room
temperature. To the resulting homogeneous orange-yellow solution was
added (MeO)3SiPh (224 µL, 1.20 mmol), TBAF (2.3 mL, 2.3 mmol), and the
alkyl bromide (1.00 mmol). The reaction mixture was stirred vigorously
for 14 hours at room temperature. The reaction mixture was then filtered
through a short pad of silica gel (washed with ~100 mL of Et2O or EtOAc),
concentrated, and purified by column chromatography.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):TITLE
$DATUM Room-Temperature Hiyama Cross-Couplings of Arylsilanes with Alkyl
Bromides and Iodides
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):AUTHOR
$DATUM Lee, Jae-Young; Fu, Gregory C.
$DTYPE RXN:VAR(1):REFERENCE(1):CITATION
$DATUM Journal of the American Chemical Society (2003), 125(19), 5616-5617

