$DATUM General/Typical Procedure: General procedure C: Ethyl
4-((1S,2S)-2-(3-chlorophenyl)cyclopropyl)benzoate (8b)
1-Fluoro-3-((1S,2S)-2-(4-nitrophenyl)cyclopropyl)benzene (8c) The product
was synthesized by the general procedure C using 265 mg of 6c (0.75
mmol). The crude product was purified by flash chromatography (19:1
Hexanes/Et2O, drypack) affording the desired compound (109mg, 85%) as a
yellow solid. mp: 103-105 °C Rf: 0.28 (9:1 Hexanes/EtOAc).1H-NMR (CDCl3,
300 MHz): δ 8.20-8.14 (m, 2H), 7.32-7.24 (m, 3H), 6.99-6.81 (m, 3H),
2.33-2.24 (m, 2H), 1.68-1.56 (m, 2H). 13C-NMR(CDCl3, 75 MHz): 163.0 (d, J
= 246 Hz), 150.2, 146.1, 143.9, 130.0 (d, J = 8.3 Hz), 126.1, 123.8,
121.6 (d, J = 2.1 Hz), 113.1 (d, J = 21.8 Hz), 112.5 (d, J = 21.8 Hz),
29.2, 28.2, 19.4. IR (film): 3078, 1587, 1511, 1339, 852, 688 cm-1. HRMS
(ESI, Pos) calcd for C15H13F1N1O2 [M+H]+: 258.0928 m/z, found 258.0925
m/z.
